00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260 align:start position:0%
 
Oh  at some point in our lives most of us  have probably wished we could live  forever being immortal sounds pretty  good at first essentially not aging  after a certain point being unable to  die of natural causes not a bad life but  what if everyone became immortal  overnight what if the entire worlds  population stopped dying at the current  rate approximately 150 to thousand  people die every day around the world  that's about two per second so assuming  our immortality event happens instantly  that would mean two unlucky souls would  miss it by as little as a fraction of a  second if we assume everyone stopped  dying at the time of making this video  the world population would quickly start  climbing from about seven point six  billion at the current rate about three  hundred sixty thousand people are born  each day and the current death rate  slows apparent population growth by  about 42% when this immortality event  occurred we'd begin to see dramatic  changes to our society  contrary to what you'd probably expect  overpopulation wouldn't be the first  problem we'd have to deal with if people  stopped dying the population would start  to increase more quickly but it wouldn't  become a crisis for at least a few years  one of the first negative impacts of  this change would likely be the ironic  death of the funeral industry if no one  dies of natural causes there's no one to  bury no funerals to arrange no caskets  to sell funeral homes would have to rely  on victims of violent crime car  accidents and other unnatural causes of  death to make a living  meanwhile in hospitals people sick with  formerly terminal illnesses would exist  in a permanent state of pain unable to  die and their families would be stuck  with their continued medical bills these  hospitals would begin to become  overcrowded as new patients are admitted  for various unnatural injuries and  conditions when the world begins to feel  the strain of overpopulation especially  after children are born grow up and  start having children of their own we'd  begin to see crises in several areas  first natural resources would be  depleted at an alarming rate fossil  fuels already running out today  would be used up much more quickly  forcing the world to adopt new sources  of energy to keep society running  available land supply would dwindle with  new housing springing up in any vacant  lot to accommodate the rapidly growing  population even if we could keep up with  the demand for housing young people  entering the job market would be met  with little to no opportunity for  employment all the jobs already  snatched up by those who came before  them as the unemployed begin to pile up  homelessness would become a real problem  made worse by the spike in housing  prices when space inevitably runs out  natural food would come at a premium as  land used for livestock or crops would  dwindle and suffer under the strain of  so many new mouths to feed the food  industry would have to turn to heavily  processed and cheaply manufactured food  potentially causing even more widespread  nutritional problems than we have today  with so many people out of work homeless  and hungry and with no room to spread  out  civil unrest would start building we'd  begin to see riots in the streets of  major cities anywhere there's a  concentrated population of the  unemployed on a larger scale nations  without room for their citizens may feel  the obligation to challenge their  neighbors for their territory or  resources sparking large Wars  governments would probably secretly see  these Wars as serving multiple purposes  to expand their territory and living  space but also to help thin the  population then there are more extreme  possibilities with all other options  exhausted perhaps we'd see a real-life  implementation of death sports like  those in The Hunger Games or ancient  Rome may be forced euthanasia would  become the norm for the unfit both young  and old in order to allow the healthiest  members of society to survive or more  realistically we might see stringent  restrictions on the number of children  allowed per family perhaps based on  social status occupation or income but  if we could get the population growth  under control the human race might not  be as doomed as we think we'd certainly  have to live more frugal lives and  likely have much less space to spread  out but with the right regulations in  place it could be sustainable at least  for the near future in the wake of our  new immortality we might see new  technologies developed to accommodate  the larger and longer lived population  homes designed to allow humans to live  in areas once considered undesirable  allowing the more adventurous people to  have a bit more space at the expense of  safety or convenience technological  progress would likely increase as the  demand for new innovations to help ease  the population strain would grow and  longer lives would allow scientists and  innovators more time to perform studies  and develop new ideas provided the world  didn't collapse beforehand on a personal  level we might become more creative and  artistic our longer lives allowing us to  pursue new hobbies and skills over  decades instead of limiting ourselves to  a few we'd have the chance to live  smaller mini lives living in one place  for 50 years then moving and pursuing a  new career somewhere else if the world  could sustain such a drastic change it  would be interesting to see what an  immortal society would look like of  course it's very unlikely that it would  as the strain from so many new mouths to  feed and people to house would simply be  too much  luckily immortality probably isn't  something will ever have to accommodate  and certainly not overnight what do you  think what would an immortal society  look like and what changes would you  expect to see in the world let us know  your thoughts in the comments below if  you enjoyed this video make sure to  subscribe to keep up to date with the  latest content you can watch my previous  video by clicking here or if you're  really bored you can binge watch all my  content by clicking here thanks for  watching and I'll see you next week  [Music]

